    "body": "Seconding @annevk's concerns about referencing public properties; we shouldn't be running author code to check the state.\n\nI'm not sure whether we should wait for multi-implementer interest here for this sort of cross-spec integration. (E.g. in the past we've added integration points like IntersectionObserver.) It might be clear enough to readers that this only works in browsers that have signed off on CSSImageValue. But, it would certainly make things easier to get another implementer commitment, so if you can get that, it would be much appreciated. Tagging \"needs implementer interest\" for now.\n",
